0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 87.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 14 TL (Artificial intelligence is increasingly used in workers\222 compensation claims operations to surface) Tj T* (inconsistencies, anomalies, and patterns that may warrant Special Investigations Unit \(SIU\)) Tj T* (review. However, many AI-enabled fraud detection systems fail under regulatory examination,) Tj T* (discovery, or litigation\227not due to model inaccuracy, but because their outputs are not) Tj T* (governable, reproducible, or legally defensible. In particular, unstructured communication between) Tj T* (automated systems can embed implicit accusations, omit evidence provenance, and obscure) Tj T* (accountability for decisions that affect statutory benefits.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 78 234.5 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 115.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 14 TL (This paper introduces a formal, defamation-safe, evidence-anchored communication protocol) Tj T* -0.119885 Tw (governing interactions between two AI agents: a Fraud Recommendation Agent and an SIU Triage) Tj T* 0 Tw (Agent. Designed for workers\222 compensation claims, the protocol defines message contracts,) Tj T* (evidence bundle requirements, language constraints, decision boundaries, and human-in-the-loop) Tj T* (escalation points. Rather than attempting to automate fraud adjudication, the protocol establishes) Tj T* (a systems-level governance framework that preserves investigative integrity while enabling) Tj T* (continuous learning. The contribution of this paper is a citable, enterprise-grade design pattern) Tj T* (that reframes AI-enabled SIU workflows as a coherence and accountability problem rather than a) Tj T* (prediction accuracy problem.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
 

